{
 "_doc": [
  "ROOM SIZE IS THE SIGNAL. THE BAND IS THE UNIT, NOT THE SEAT COUNT.",
  "",
  "This tool never learns how many tickets an Indian show sold — no platform publishes it.",
  "What it can see is the ROOM the promoter booked, and a promoter books a bigger room only",
  "when they believe they can fill it. Room size is therefore a revealed-preference proxy for",
  "demand, made by somebody spending their own money.",
  "",
  "Capacities below are approximate and mostly UNVERIFIED. That is deliberate and it is fine,",
  "because the code scores the BAND, not the number. 'club' -> 'theatre_mid' is a real",
  "escalation whether the theatre seats 900 or 1,200; a 30% error in the seat count does not",
  "change the band. Anything that depends on the exact number is a bug.",
  "",
  "Unknown venues are the common case, not the exception. classify_venue() falls back to",
  "keyword patterns, and a venue it cannot place at all gets band null — which propagates as",
  "'unknown', never as 'small'. An unmeasured room must not read as a weak one."
 ],
